  "refinements": [
    "Public reverse selected rather than unchecked primitive: original diagnostic argument, error distinction, optional force/check features and explicit return/poll semantics",
    "Hand-designed complete compilation path with early semantic lineage/export and completed GVM obligations before old C scanning; no emitted GVM or generated Zig claimed",
    "Worked DispatchHostProfile using local iteration and explicit VM dispositions; TailHostProfile remains separately admitted alternative with no binary mixture or incidental tail-optimization assumption",
    "Actual no-handles isolated cons B=3 conditioned on no hidden allocation, valid interval rights, headroom and provenance; stored post-cons schedule preserved with roots/completion/current binding",
    "Heap-section change, GC relocation, force/capture/error and return semantics distinguished; native temporaries, Zig defer and C imports supply no automatic Scheme roots/control",
    "Common _std module manifest retains unique definitions and init ownership; one function does not qualify the entire library or justify linking duplicated old/new exports",
    "Explicit image/VM binding, point/frame/constant/code users and failed/cyclic/reentrant initialization custody; old fixup flag is not transactional publication evidence",
    "Six dependency-ordered retirement obligations, eight maintenance events and matched report matrix; modern generated C and common LLVM services credited before residual Zig cost",
    "Gambit modernization continues through language-independent semantic/runtime contracts and independent LLVM provider if Zig economics fail; modern C remains a valid carrier",
    "Eight handwritten implications, sixteen logical counterexamples and ten unevaluated control cases; no checked proof, runtime witness, path retirement or positive economic gate"
  ],
